# Frontend build context exclusions.
#
# Governs `context: ./frontend`. Without it the builder uploads `node_modules/` — typically
# 300+ MB — on every build, and `npm ci` then overwrites it anyway. Excluding it is both a large
# speed-up and a correctness fix: the image's dependencies come from `package-lock.json` alone,
# never from whatever happens to be on the developer's disk.

# ---- Dependencies (reinstalled by `npm ci` inside the builder) ----
node_modules/

# ---- Build output (regenerated by `vite build` inside the builder) ----
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Secrets ----
# VITE_* values are compiled into the bundle, so a stray .env here would be baked in and served
# to every browser. The API base URL is passed explicitly as a build argument instead.
.env
.env.*

# ---- Test / coverage output ----
coverage/

# ---- VCS / editor ----
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
